{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_today_weather", "description": "Retrieves the today's weather data based on location.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"location": {"type": "string", "description": "the location for retieving the weather data."}}, "required": ["location"]}, "return": {"type": "object", "description": "A dictionary containing the status and today's weather data."}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_future_weather", "description": "Retrieves the location's weather for a future timestamp.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"location": {"type": "string", "description": "the location for retieving the weather data."}, "start_time": {"type": "string", "description": "The start timestamp for the future weather(format: 'YYYY-MM-DD', e.g. 2024-05-28)."}, "end_time": {"type": "string", "description": "The end timestamp for the future weather(format: 'YYYY-MM-DD', e.g. 2024-05-29)."}}, "required": ["location", "start_time", "end_time"]}, "return": {"type": "object", "description": "A dictionary containing the status and the future weather data."}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "search_news_by_category", "description": "Finds the news by category.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"category": {"type": "string", "description": "The category to search for news. should shoose from [entertainment, world, business, sport, health, science, technology]"}}, "required": ["category"]}, "return": {"type": "object", "description": "A dictionary contains the search status and the search result"}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "search_heat_news", "description": "Fetches the latest hot news articles.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {}}, "return": {"type": "object", "description": "A dictionary contains the search status and search result."}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "search_from_wikipedia", "description": "Searches Wikipedia for content based on a given query and returns the top k results.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "The search term to look for on Wikipedia."}, "topk": {"type": "integer", "description": "The number of top results to return. Defaults to 5."}}, "required": ["query"]}, "return": {"type": "object", "description": "A dictionary containing the search status and the processed search results. The 'data' field contains a list of processed paragraphs, each in the format \"title
truncated content\"."}}}
</tools>

For each function call, return a json object with function name and arguments within <tool_call></tool_call> XML tags:
<tool_call>
{"name": <function-name>, "arguments": <args-json-object>}
</tool_call>

